{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"After rollback, the older daemon can merge an entry that was held for human approval without that approval."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"normal","reason":"An entry waiting for approval occupies the repository's single land slot and can leave other PRs stuck behind it for days."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A failed poll can leave a dismissed approval in the saved snapshot, allowing the factory to proceed without current approval."},{"id":"F4","consequence":"bypass","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A bot's approval can satisfy the check described as requiring another person's approval, although it meets the specified account-based predicate."},{"id":"F5","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An entry already past its push can merge without an approval lookup after the policy is enabled, and a later dismissal also goes unchecked."},{"id":"F6","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A proxy left running across an upgrade rejects the new state and fails status and run-inspection requests."}]}